\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O little town of Bethlehem,
\par How still we see thee lie!
\par Above thy deep and dreamless sleep
\par The silent stars go by:
\par Yet in Thy dark street shineth
\par The everlasting Light;
\par The hopes and fears of all the years
\par Are met in thee to-night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O morning stars, together
\par Proclaim the holy birth,
\par And praises sing to God the King,
\par And peace to men on earth;
\par For Christ is born of Mary,
\par And, gathered all above,
\par While mortals sleep, the angels keep,
\par Their watch of wondering love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. How silently, how silently
\par The wondrous gift is given!
\par So God imparts to human hearts
\par The blessings of His heaven.
\par No ear may hear His coming;
\par But in this world of sin,
\par Where meek souls will receive Him, still
\par The dear Christ enters in.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O holy Child of Bethlehem,
\par Descend to us, we pray;
\par Cast out our sin, and enter in;
\par Be born in us-today.
\par We hear the Christmas angels
\par The great glad tidings tell;
\par O come to us, abide with us,
\par Our Lord Immanuel.
\par                        Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

